// RPC-transport counterpart to `riverpod_shared_type_orphan.cstack`, for
// cratestack#628's acceptance criterion that the zero-procedure
// `procedures.dart` import/part-directive gates be verified under both
// `transport rest` (the default, exercised by the sibling fixture) and
// `transport rpc` — `rest_procedures.dart.j2`/`rpc_procedures.dart.j2`
// are two separate templates carrying the fix independently (unlike
// `build_procedures.rs`'s import computation, which is transport-agnostic
// and shared by both), so the AC asks for this to be exercised literally
// rather than argued from the code.
//
// Same shape as the REST fixture: zero procedures, and `Coordinates` is a
// `type` block referenced by nothing (no *stored* model field can ever
// be typed with a `type` block — parser-enforced, only a `@computed`
// field is exempt, and no field below carries one), so it's an orphan
// that `partition::Owner::owner_by_name` defaults to `Owner::Shared`
// rather than `Owner::Procedures`. That keeps `procedures.dart`'s own
// `data_classes` empty too, giving a true zero-procedure,
// zero-data-class `procedures.dart` under `transport rpc`.

transport rpc

model Widget {
  id Int @id
  name String
}

type Coordinates {
  lat Float
  lng Float
}
